Subject: Fix: physics contacts no longer start from stack leftovers
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A fix of the original game, always on and without a switch. It lives in the
tweak series so the faithful series stays retail.

PhysicsWorld::SpaceCollideCallback collects up to 20 contacts in an
uninitialized stack array. dCollide fills only each contact's geometry; the
objects' Contact() then set some surface parameters (bounce, mu, soft_cfm,
...) but none ever assigns surface.mode: they only set or clear flags in it.
The mode ODE applies (bounce, second friction, friction direction, slip,
softness) and every parameter no Contact() sets therefore came from whatever
the stack held. On the Wii the same code left the same leftovers on every
console, so lockstep matches agreed; natively the leftovers depend on the
compiler, the operating system and the calls made before, and the contact
joints differed between two runs of the same step (found by the rollback
sync test: ODE's contact joint arena and AI fuzzy variables differed after a
replay while the game's checksum still matched). The goalie's ball contact
in PhysicsAIBall::CheckIfBallWentThroughGoalie has the same uninitialized
dContact.

Both now start zeroed: a contact's flags and parameters are exactly those the
game sets. Where a leftover happened to enable a flag, contacts behave
slightly differently from the original; no single native value could
reproduce every Wii's leftovers.

diff --git a/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp b/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp
index ae9f3d7..b8b340c 100644
--- a/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Physics/PhysicsWorld.cpp
@@ -148,6 +148,14 @@ void PhysicsWorld::SpaceCollideCallback(void* data, dxGeom* geom1, dxGeom* geom2
 
     dContact* contact;
     dContact contacts[20];
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // Port fix, always on: dCollide fills only each contact's geometry, and no
+    // Contact() ever assigns surface.mode (they only set or clear flags in it)
+    // nor every surface parameter. The original used whatever the stack held,
+    // so the contact flags ODE applies (bounce, second friction, slip, ...)
+    // depended on earlier calls: the same on every Wii, not on every PC.
+    memset(contacts, 0, sizeof(contacts));
+#endif
     dBodyID body1;
 
     body1 = dGeomGetBody(geom1);
diff --git a/src/Game/PhysicsAIBall.cpp b/src/Game/PhysicsAIBall.cpp
index bcddb6f..e96a258 100644
--- a/src/Game/PhysicsAIBall.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/PhysicsAIBall.cpp
@@ -419,6 +419,11 @@ void PhysicsAIBall::CheckIfBallWentThroughGoalie()
         SetPosition(ballPosition, WORLD_COORDINATES);
 
         dContact contactInfo;
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+        // Port fix, always on: no stack leftovers in the goalie contact's
+        // unset fields (see PhysicsWorld::SpaceCollideCallback).
+        contactInfo = dContact();
+#endif
         SetContactInfo(&contactInfo, pGoalie->m_pPhysicsCharacter, true);
 
         contactInfo.geom.normal[0] = contactNormal.x;
